  "verdict": "PASS \u2014 the THIRD human-disease arm (common/complex/polygenic), popularity-CONTROLLED. Genetically-supported genes are enriched for approved/clinical drug targets genome-wide: Fisher OR=2.26 (p=1.2e-63; MH-by-disease OR=2.06), dose-responsive to OR=5.1838 at genetic_association>0.5. The enrichment SURVIVES the study-attention null: controlling for gene publication count, fame-adjusted Mantel-Haenszel OR=1.67 (p=1.6e-31; crosses OR>2 at genetic>0.2), fame-matched permutation p=1.0e-04, logistic genetic coef=0.090 (p=3.2e-37) beyond fame and =0.058 (p=5.9e-16) beyond fame+literature. Generalizes: 27/27 leave-one-disease-out folds, 27/27 per-disease OR>1. HONEST ATTENUATION: popularity explains a substantial share of the crude effect (OR 2.26 -> fame-adjusted 1.67); the popularity-free effect is bounded between these (adjustment partly over-controls a collider), and only strong genetic support clears OR>2 after adjustment. SCOPE: in-silico target-RELEVANCE via genetics (Open Targets 26.06, cross-sectional); NOT drug-response, NOT a molecule, NOT clinical efficacy. Contribution = popularity-controlled complex-disease arm + honest abstention where genetic evidence is absent. Intervention still hits the affinity wall (HIT2/B49/B65). A fully clean causal test of Nelson-2015 needs a temporal/prospective design not runnable on this snapshot."
